__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Per-device material and local build output are never part of the source repo.
# HANDOVER.md is one session's note to the next -- where the work stands, which
# port the device is on, what to build next. It names this machine's paths and
# addresses, so check-private-data.py reports it, and rightly: an untracked file
# that nothing ignores is a file `git add -A` would publish.
/HANDOVER.md
/RELEASE-PLAN.md
/private/
/vendor-private/
/device-assets/
/backups/
/work/
/out/
/build-share/
# wrangler, run for the site from this directory, caches the Cloudflare account
# it is signed in to -- .wrangler/cache/wrangler-account.json holds the account
# id and name. Untracked and unignored, it is a file `git add -A` would publish,
# and the first commit of the open-source folder is exactly such an add
# (found 2026-10-30 while checking that export).
# Unanchored on purpose: `/.wrangler/` only matches the one at the repo root,
# and wrangler writes one wherever it is run from. Kept after the site moved out
# of this tree on 2026-10-31 (it is its own project now), because the cost is a
# line and what it prevents is publishing the account it is signed in to --
# anyone who runs wrangler from inside this tree once would otherwise leave that
# file untracked and unignored. Checked with `git check-ignore -v` rather than
# by reading the pattern.
.wrangler/
# Nothing in this tree has one today, and the site that did is no longer in it --
# but 193 MB of somebody else's code is the one mistake a first `git add -A`
# must not be able to make.
node_modules/
emmc-*.bin
*.wbf
*.wbf.gz
*.pem
*.jks
adbkey*
system.img
userdata.img
*.raw.img
*.img
*.bin
*.ko
*.odex
*.vdex
*.oat
*.art

# Other projects' releases the image carries unmodified are fetched, not kept:
# tools/fetch-prebuilts.py (list: device/amazon/pw3/apps/prebuilts.json).
*.apk
.fetch-*
